                <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">Without prices, leaving things to the market means someone gets hurt and essential services go unprovided. <strong>Microeconomics</strong> calls this 'market failure,' and addressing it is the starting point for <strong>macroeconomic</strong> policy.</p>
