                <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">We always feel anxious when buying things. "Is this used car just shiny on the outside but actually flood-damaged?" "Is this financial product really good for me?" Economics calls this <strong>Information Asymmetry</strong>—when one party in a transaction has much more information than the other.</p>
